+
+# Validate task title, priority and tag input
+
+## Request
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, and odd tasks show up. The list must
+reject invalid input with a clear error that says what is wrong:
+
+- a title that is empty, or only spaces;
+- a title longer than 120 characters;
+- a priority other than `low`, `normal` and `high`;
+- a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+This applies when a task is added, renamed or tagged. When input is rejected, nothing in the list
+changes.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Feature: task list for the Tidy Tasks app (`README.md`).
+- Requirement: the list rejects invalid titles, priorities and tags with an error that says what is
+  wrong, and a rejected change leaves the list as it was.
+- Acceptance: see the request above; covered by tests in `test/list.test.ts`.
+
+## Design
+
+- A new error code, `invalid-input`, joins `TodoErrorCode` in `src/domain/result.ts`. The other codes
+  do not fit: `not-found`, `duplicate` and `invalid-state` describe the list, not the input.
+- The checks live in `src/domain/task.ts`, each returning a `Result`: `checkTitle`, `checkPriority`,
+  `checkTag`, and `checkNewTask`, which applies the title, priority and tag checks to an `add` input.
+- `add` runs `checkNewTask` first; `rename` runs `checkTitle` on the new title; `tag` runs `checkTag`
+  on the tag. Each check runs before the list looks anything up or reads the clock, so a rejected
+  change touches nothing.
+- Title: trimmed first, then the empty check and the length check apply to the trimmed title. The
+  length counts characters (code points), not UTF-16 units, so an emoji counts as one.
+- Priority: matched exactly against `PRIORITIES`; no trimming and no case folding.
+- Tag: a tag that is only spaces, or empty, is reported as empty. A tag containing whitespace is
+  rejected as containing a space; this includes a tab, which the request does not name but which would
+  split a tag in the same way.
+- `untag` and `remove` are not changed: a tag that could not have been added cannot be on a task.
+- The error messages name the problem and the limit, e.g. `a title can be at most 120 characters, this
+  one has 130`, and `priority must be low, normal or high, not "urgent"`.
+
+## Notes
+
+- No credentials or secrets are involved.
+- Public API change: `TodoErrorCode` gains `invalid-input`. Additive for existing callers that match on
+  the code; callers that switch on it exhaustively must handle the new case.
